### =====================================================================
### EnerDeFi mock providers: test control panel
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and Visual Studio 2022 (17.12+).
### In JetBrains Rider, everything works except the automatic @jobId; paste a job id in by hand.
### Start the mocks first:  dotnet run --project providers/MockProviders
### =====================================================================

@admin = http://localhost:5100


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Overview and status
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### What the control panel offers
GET {{admin}}/

### Mode and call count of each provider (compare call counts to see where your API routed checks)
GET {{admin}}/admin/status


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### QuickVerify modes
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### QuickVerify: Normal (default: ~30% failures, ~10% slow)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Normal

### QuickVerify: Healthy (never fails, never slow)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Healthy

### QuickVerify: Slow (every response takes 5 seconds)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Slow

### QuickVerify: Down (every request returns 503)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Down


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### SureCheck modes
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### SureCheck: Normal
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Normal

### SureCheck: Healthy
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Healthy

### SureCheck: Slow
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Slow

### SureCheck: Down
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Down


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### TrustLink modes
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### TrustLink: Normal (~10% submit failures, webhooks in 3-10 s, ~15% duplicates, ~10% "issuer unavailable")
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Normal

### TrustLink: Healthy (no failures, webhooks in 2-4 s, no duplicates)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Healthy

### TrustLink: Slow (webhooks take 30 seconds)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Slow

### TrustLink: Down (submissions return 503)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Down


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Scenarios
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Scenario: everything healthy (run all three)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Healthy

###
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Healthy

###
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Healthy

### Scenario: primary outage. QuickVerify down; checks should still complete elsewhere
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Down

### Scenario: async provider outage. TrustLink down; what does the candidate's API do?
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Down

### Scenario: total outage (run all three). Project should stay unverified with a clear "try later" response
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Down

###
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Down

###
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Down

### Scenario: reset everything to Normal (run all three)
PUT {{admin}}/admin/quickverify/mode/Normal

###
PUT {{admin}}/admin/surecheck/mode/Normal

###
PUT {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/mode/Normal


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### TrustLink webhooks
### Trigger a verification through the candidate's API first, so there is a webhook to work with.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Recent webhook deliveries (newest first) and how the candidate's API responded.
### Look for kind = "duplicate" and check each event was only processed once.
# @name deliveries
GET {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/webhooks

### The TrustLink job id from the newest delivery above (run "deliveries" first).
### To target a different job, replace the value with any trustLinkJobId from the list.
@jobId = {{deliveries.response.body.$[0].trustLinkJobId}}

### Forged webhook: same payload, signature made with the wrong secret.
### Expect responseStatus 401 or 403, and the project must not change.
POST {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/webhooks/{{jobId}}/forged

### Replay: re-sends the last delivery with its ORIGINAL timestamp and signature.
### Within 5 minutes of the original: accepted, but must not be processed twice.
### After 5 minutes: should be rejected as stale.
POST {{admin}}/admin/trustlink/webhooks/{{jobId}}/replay
